The board of water, light and sinking fund commissioners, the duly constituted city agency and instrumentality having control, direction and supervision of its water system, shall begin the addition of fluoride to the public water supply after the local and state health authorities have approved the addition of fluoride and have:
(1) Established reasonable maximum and minimum limits of fluoride, stated in parts per million, to be maintained in the public water supply;
(2) Approved the type of chemical feeding equipment to be installed and used;
(3) Approved the installation of the equipment, plant layout and methods of handling the fluoride compound to ensure the safety of employees;
(4) Approved the method of analysis and control to be used in determining the fluoride content of the water before and after the addition of fluoride; and
(5) Established a method of providing for the cost of acquisition, installation, operation and maintenance of fluoride equipment, fluoride compound and all other attendant costs.
(Code 1983, § 27-24)
